      "text": "To find the area of a triangle with vertices \\((0,0)\\), \\((0,5)\\), and \\((7,12)\\), we can use the formula for the area of a triangle given its vertices \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given coordinates \\((x_1, y_1) = (0, 0)\\), \\((x_2, y_2) = (0, 5)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3) = (7, 12)\\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(5 - 12) + 0(12 - 0) + 7(0 - 5) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the absolute value:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 7(-5) \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -35 \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 35\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 17.5\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{17.5}\\) square units.",
