      "text": "We can use the Shoelace Theorem to find the area of the triangle.\nThe Shoelace Theorem states that if the vertices of a polygon are given by $((x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \\dots, (x_n, y_n))$, then the area of the polygon is given by:\n$$\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| \\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i y_{i+1} - y_i x_{i+1}) \\right|$$\nwhere $x_{n+1} = x_1$ and $y_{n+1} = y_1$.\nIn this case, the vertices of the triangle are $(0,0)$, $(0,5)$, and $(7,12)$.\nPlugging these values into the Shoelace Theorem, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| (0 \\cdot 5 - 0 \\cdot 12) + (0 \\cdot 12 - 5 \\cdot 7) + (7 \\cdot 0 - 12 \\cdot 0) \\right| \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + (-35) + 0 \\right| \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -35 \\right| \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{17.5}\n\\end{align*}\nSo the area of the triangle is $\\boxed{17.5}$ square units.The answer is: 17.5",
